# Intent: one link screen for every state where the unit is not yet linked (owner, 2026-11-13). A black cover with a glyph slot (the shipped Wi-Fi icons, drawn 1.5 times, the bars cycling while it connects) and a text slot: "Connecting to Wi-Fi...", "Wi-Fi setup needed" with the hotspot name and the address from the existing setup flow (one line each; the mint face has no speech bubble, so the setup text was never visible), "Connecting to Home...", and "Waiting for Home to approve me" (the slash glyph and a key drawn from shapes). It replaces patch 033's boot cover, its blue blink and its dim white ring at the first Standby: the ring is dark at boot and blinks cyan only while Wi-Fi setup or approval waits for a person. ShowBootCover, HideBootCover and BootRingTick are gone; ApplyLink() is the one place that picks the look. Wi-Fi setup always shows the screen, also when asked after boot.
# Upstream: m5stack/StackChan firmware/main/hal/board/stackchan_display.cc and stackchan_display.h (MIT). Applies after 110.
# Check after a flash: power on: black screen, Wi-Fi bars cycling, "Connecting to Wi-Fi...", then "Connecting to Home...", the ring stays dark and no white ring appears when the face comes up. With no saved Wi-Fi: "Wi-Fi setup needed", the hotspot name and the address, a cyan ring blink, and the captive setup page still opens from the hotspot.
